WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.894
1Password was breached

00:00:01.706 --> 00:00:02.708
through an employee's

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.522
GitHub account

00:00:04.062 --> 00:00:05.595
On November 19

00:00:05.831 --> 00:00:07.505
1Password found signs

00:00:07.317 --> 00:00:08.295
that an attacker

00:00:08.119 --> 00:00:09.038
had entered an

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.099
employee's corporate

00:00:09.911 --> 00:00:10.925
GitHub account

00:00:11.446 --> 00:00:12.471
The attacker used

00:00:12.283 --> 00:00:12.979
it to reach

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:13.780
source code and

00:00:13.592 --> 00:00:14.806
push malicious code

00:00:14.654 --> 00:00:15.915
to backend services

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.436
which downloaded customer

00:00:17.248 --> 00:00:17.849
names

00:00:18.085 --> 00:00:19.570
email addresses and

00:00:19.382 --> 00:00:20.986
internal account metadata

00:00:21.518 --> 00:00:22.838
Customer vault contents

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:23.864
were never accessed

00:00:23.959 --> 00:00:25.244
and 1Password says

00:00:25.056 --> 00:00:26.046
its design means

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:26.588
a breach of

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.602
its systems cannot

00:00:27.414 --> 00:00:29.053
expose vault contents

00:00:29.574 --> 00:00:30.588
Full story on

00:00:30.399 --> 00:00:31.295
the dashboard
